  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the given compounds:&nbsp;</p><p>(1)&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0134_bdbe1ed5511d.png\" style=\"width: 183px; height: 65px;\" />;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> on Nitrogen is&nbsp;delocalised.</p><p>(2)&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0134_577ab1f76741.png\" style=\"width: 211px; height: 73px;\" />;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> on Nitrogen is&nbsp;localised.</p><p>(3)&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0134_a8dae7abba6e.png\" style=\"width: 211px; height: 68px;\" />;&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> on Nitrogen is&nbsp;delocalised due to conjugation with both&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\st0134_32e720452b8a.png\" style=\"width: 54px; height: 59px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>(Hence least basic)</p><p>(4) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#168;</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> on Nitrogen&nbsp;is localised.</p>"
